    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Utriculariagraminifolia(049BTC)/4480",
      "html": "<p>Utricularia graminifolia from Asia belongs to the bladderwort family. All the plants in this family are insect eating, perennial water and marsh plants. In nature, the plant lives in nutrient-poor places, hence the need to catch small insects and digest them. Bladder traps are a unique feature of this family, which Utricularia graminifolia forms after a short period in the aquarium. The species name means 'with grass like leaves' and the fresh green leaves will after some time form a pretty mat which looks like a lawn (2-8 cm tall). Utricularia graminifolia is therefore an ideal foreground plant, although it is rather demanding.</p>"
    }
  ],
